  "query_preview": "(Today through Saturday)...\nIssued at 1216 AM EST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nAn abrupt change for the holiday week arrives later today with a \ncold front pushing through the area this afternoon, accompanied by a \nperiod of widespread showers and breezy conditions.\n\nTemperatures will turn sharply cooler this week, though they will \nonly be near to slightly below normals, which for Indy are currently \nin the upper 40s for highs and low 30s for lows.\n\nRain may be briefly heavy at times this afternoon and evening, with \nprecipitable water values approaching climatological maximum due in \npart to remnant Pacific moisture accompanying the frontal system, \nbut very dry antecedent conditions and limited rainfall time will \nprevent any significant concerns from this. Dry weather will quickly \nreturn late tomorrow night into Monday as another strong surface \nridge pushes through the area.\n\nA complex forecast scenario then evolves for mid to late week as \nmodels depict a couple of closed lows possibly merging Wednesday \ninto Thursday as they push eastward through the Ohio and Tennessee \nValleys. Model differences remain fairly substantial with their \nhandling of this scenario, though this will require at least chance \nPoPs from late Wednesday into Thanksgiving. Temperatures should be \nwarm enough for the bulk of this to fall as rain, but a few flakes \nmixing in cannot be ruled out for any precip falling during the \nnight when temperatures drop. The vast majority of actual impacts \nfrom this system, however, look to be well east of the area as the \nupper level low produces strong cyclogenesis along the potent \ncoastal baroclinic zone.",
